{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0019827","isObsolete":false,"name":"stem cell population maintenance","definition":{"text":"The process by which an organism or tissue maintains a population of stem cells of a single type. This can be achieved by a number of mechanisms: stem cell asymmetric division maintains stem cell numbers; stem cell symmetric division increases them; maintenance of a stem cell niche maintains the conditions for commitment to the stem cell fate for some types of stem cell; stem cells may arise de novo from other cell types.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"ISBN","dbId":"0878932437"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"maintenance of pluripotency","type":"related"}],"replaces":[{"id":"GO:1904671","type":"consider"}],"children":[{"id":"GO:0010074","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0097150","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:1902455","relation":"negatively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:1902459","relation":"positively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:0035019","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:2000036","relation":"regulates"},{"id":"GO:0030718","relation":"is_a"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process by which an organism or tissue maintains a population of stem cells of a single type. This can be achieved by a number of mechanisms: stem cell asymmetric division maintains stem cell numbers; stem cell symmetric division increases them; maintenance of a stem cell niche maintains the conditions for commitment to the stem cell fate for some types of stem cell; stem cells may arise de novo from other cell types."},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The pr